 S<VDDK 6.7> (https://bugzilla.redhat.com/1901489).  Upgrade to at
 least S<VDDK 7> to resolve the issue.
 
+=head1 INPUT FROM NFC
+
+Use the nbdkit-nfc-plugin to connect to NFC port 902, which is a free
+alternative to VDDK.  It works similarly to F<-it vddk>
+
+Basic usage is:
+
+ $ virt-v2v \
+     -ic 'vpx://root@vcenter.example.com/Datacenter/esxi?no_verify=1' \
+     -it nfc \
+     "Windows 2003" \
+     -o local -os /var/tmp
+
 =head1 INPUT FROM VMWARE OVA
 
 Virt-v2v is able to import guests from VMware’s OVA (Open
